#:layer #!pragmatics

^["intent"]{
  ~#goal: "Start with dumb register cells (value + address), then progressively enrich cells by phase (lex -> parse -> sem -> opt -> prag) while adding operational/positional register semantics for query/runtime coherence."
  ~#taste: "clarity, layering, expressiveness"
}

^["stream"]{
  >> [2026-02-27 01:28] observe — runtime register bank already supports descriptor/provenance/lens but lacks explicit phase progression structure.
  >> [2026-02-27 01:28] observe — brace register dyad behavior is documented, yet cursor/open-close capture flow is not wired in code.
  >> [2026-02-27 01:28] decide — preserve existing register APIs (`set/get/yank/paste`) and add phase facets as additive metadata, not a breaking schema reset.
  >> [2026-02-27 01:28] decide — split selector semantics into operational and positional dimensions to reduce ambiguity for projection/reduction/objective/subjective queries.
  >> [2026-02-27 01:28] taste — prefer a minimal invariant core with optional enrichment per stage, so early pipeline stays deterministic and cheap.
  >> [2026-02-27 01:31] decide — keep `parse` and `sem` as coarse buckets for this increment.
  >> [2026-02-27 01:31] decide — selector surface is Spw-native grammar first (not preset-only aliases).
  >> [2026-02-27 01:31] decide — phase enrichment is in-place on existing cells; lineage edges remain optional metadata.
  >> [2026-02-27 01:46] ship — types: RegisterPhase, PhaseFacet (memoryWeight), PhaseEnvelope (evictable), RegisterAddress, PHASE_ORDER
  >> [2026-02-27 01:46] ship — RegisterBank: enrichPhase(), phaseOf(), phase-aware set(), advancePhase() with weight
  >> [2026-02-27 01:46] ship — 5 new tests: progressive enrichment, phase-annotated set, unphased cells, memoryWeight derivation, snapshot immutability
  >> [2026-02-27 01:46] taste — progressive enhancement: facets additive, value preserved through enrichment. Spw serialization: phase maps 1:1 to !phase[] modifier tags. memory granularity: PHASE_ORDER drives eviction priority.
}

